Oneko pet pack — provenance & license
======================================

These PNG frames (oneko-*.png) are per-pose slices of the classic "Neko"
desktop-pet sprite sheet (oneko.gif), sliced into this project's pet-frame
naming scheme (idle / happy / sleepy / sleeping / thinking / surprised / sad /
celebrating / walk1-4).

Source sprite sheet
-------------------
- File:    oneko.gif (256x128, an 8x4 grid of 32px tiles)
- From:    https://github.com/adryd325/oneko.js  (main branch)
- The oneko.js *code* is MIT-licensed: Copyright (c) 2022 adryd.
- The *sprite art* is the original "Neko" screen-mate artwork, first written for
  the NEC PC-9801 in 1989. It is ancient and universally treated as PUBLIC
  DOMAIN (see e.g. https://github.com/glreno/oneko — "The image files are
  ancient public domain"; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neko_(software)).

How these frames were produced
------------------------------
The tile coordinates come directly from oneko.js's `spriteSets` map ([col,row]
into the 32px grid). Each pose was cropped to a standalone 32x32 RGBA PNG and
mapped onto Tofu's expression names (a cat has poses, not emotions, so the
mapping is closest-pose: alert->happy, tired->sleepy, grooming->thinking,
scratch-wall->celebrating/surprised, the E-run pair->walk1-4, sleeping->sleeping,
sleeping-frame2->sad).

Why it is safe to ship in the open-source export
------------------------------------------------
Both the code license (MIT) and the art (public domain) permit redistribution,
including commercially, with attribution. This file is that attribution. These
are normal committed source assets — NOT `.tofu*` agent artifacts — and are
intended to be included in every export mode.
